    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: a1a4eec4740185a97a47a053e26b764f3931a969 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge** (review of the head a1a4eec4; the two own commits 62d8b7dd and a1a4eec4 were read against #972's head 2f29aad0).\n\n**What looks good**\n- The commits under this PR's own two are exactly the diff from #972's head (2f29aad0 is #972's head, OPEN). The own change is xtask-only plus `docs/decisions/1021-path-included-modules.md` and `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` (19 to 20).\n- Mapping is a union: `quick.rs` keeps the old `(module, submodule)` push and adds the `#[path]` parent pair on top, so a file never selects fewer suites. The earlier narrowing (`*_tests.rs`) is gone.\n- Parser (`xtask/src/path_mods.rs`): no `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` outside tests (the `unwrap_or` calls cannot panic); the `rest[..dir_end]` slice splits on an ASCII `/`; a missing directory or unreadable file returns `Ok(None)`; `//` comments are stripped before matching.\n- Tests: `a_path_included_file_selects_its_parents_submodule_suites` pins `index_swing` and the four previously dropped suites (`wall_column_gouge`, `contour_arc_sim`, `rest_across_setups`, `plasma_gate`).\n- `Changelog: none` and `Fixes #1021` are in the body.\n\n**Local results** (worktree at a1a4eec4, trial merge with current origin/main, clean)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p xtask` | 45 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run` | falls back to batch: the diff vs origin/main includes `Cargo.toml` (carried by the #965/#967/#972 commits and main's own moves), so the plan is the full batch (9 steps, 0 failed) |\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base 2f29aad0 --dry-run` | same batch fallback (the trial-merged tree differs from #972 in `Cargo.toml`); the PR's own six files are all under `xtask/`, `.claude/`, `docs/` |\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n1. GitHub's base for this PR is `main`, but its branch carries the #965, #967 and #972 commits (`git log origin/main..HEAD`). Merging it as is merges that stack too. #972 is still open, so merge #972 first (or retarget as the stacking law says) and expect this branch to take the cleaner diff after.\n2. `path_mods.rs` indexes `s[1]` and `c[1]` on regex captures. The group is mandatory in both patterns, so it cannot panic; `.get(1)` would just be the house style for \"indexing safe\".\n3. `PROCESS_VERSION` 20 is correct after the stack; main is at 16, so whichever merges second takes the next number, as the process allows.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
